# 36. PROCEDURAL BUILDING QUALITY

If the environment is generated through Lua/Luau:

Do not generate everything from identical cubes.

Create reusable construction functions for:

* houses
* apartments
* shops
* streetlights
* fences
* trees
* benches
* stadium structures
* signs
* windows
* doors

Use variation parameters:

```text
building width
building height
roof type
window layout
material
color
balcony
entrance
decoration
```

This allows procedural generation while avoiding repetitive geometry.

---

# 37. MODELING STRATEGY

Where Roblox-native geometry is sufficient:

Use Parts / MeshParts / Terrain appropriately.

Where simple geometry looks too primitive:

Use more detailed MeshParts or suitable Roblox-compatible assets.

Do not depend on random free assets that could introduce:

* malware/scripts
* poor optimization
* inconsistent art style
* copyright problems

Any external assets must be reviewed before use.

---

# 38. PERFORMANCE

Visual quality must not destroy performance.

Target:

* PC
* lower-end mobile
* mid-range mobile

Use:

* Instance Streaming
* reasonable part counts
* reusable assets
* object pooling
* LOD where appropriate
* optimized particles
* limited transparency
* limited dynamic lights
* efficient NPC simulation

Do not place hundreds of unique high-cost objects everywhere.

---

# 39. QUALITY SETTINGS

Prepare a scalable graphics system.

Quality levels:

```text
LOW
MEDIUM
HIGH
ULTRA
```

Control:

* particles
* trails
* VFX
* lighting
* post-processing
* NPC detail
* environmental detail where appropriate

Low-end players should still get the complete game.

They should simply receive reduced visual complexity.

